factcheck by anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5: 5 problems
  The reel_script and slides_spec say the Neelambur flyover 'is to be built' / 'will be constructed', which is roughly consistent, but the article says the flyover is 'already in use' only for the 10 km stretch; the draft's framing is acceptable. However, the reel_script says 'நீலாம்பூர் சந்திப்பில் புதிய மேம்பாலம் கட்டப்பட உள்ளது' while the article says the project is still at design/survey stage with a consultancy preparing a map, so 'will be built' is stated as settled rather than planned.
  The reel_script states the flyover design 'should be designed' so vehicles from Salem bypass turn left/right easily, but it omits that the design is still being finalized and a map is being prepared by a consultancy.
  The article says the Tamil Nadu ruling party (த.வெ.க.) inclusion is in the highway department's action plan; the draft's slide 'அடுத்த கட்டம்' says the flyover work will start from Coldwins area, which the article only says is the point where the survey took measurements, not a confirmed start date or decision.
  The reel_script omits the airport-side detail that a separate entry-exit ramp for airport-bound traffic is planned (the article mentions a dedicated descent platform), keeping only the tunnel and separate path.
